      "content": "i get that but i'm not really looking for a doctor right now, i just want to optimize my nutrition. i've seen some people in biohacking forums talking about high dose protocols, like taking 100mg or even 200mg of elemental iron a day to really see a difference in energy. is that like a normal range for someone trying to fix a deficiency fast? i just want to know if that kind of amount is something that actually works for optimization.",
