      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High doses of iron are not typically recommended for optimization or biohacking purposes. The recommended daily intake of elemental iron varies by age and sex, but the Tolerable Upper Intake Level (UL) is 45 mg per day for adult men and 40 mg per day for adult women. Taking 100mg or 200mg of elemental iron per day is above the UL and may cause digestive issues, stomach pain, and other complications. It's unlikely that high doses would work faster or better for addressing fatigue.",
